A||||8||zeusrekning||Need ebay bidding help.||||1||
Z||000000||zeusrekning||12-07-2000||10:28 PM||||I want to bid on some cycle parts but have never done so.<BR>The bid has not moved in a few days and i really need the parts.<BR>How long should i wait to bid?<BR>any other "Secrets"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-07-2000||10:56 PM||||My experience witheBat is to either bid high enough to discourage others if you really want/need the item, or wait till the last 10-15 minutes of the auction and bid it up hoping the other bidders don't have time to check and possibly raise their bids.<P>You also need to be careful on eBay, sometimes you can find good deals, other times I see people paying more that for a new part directly from GM.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||12-07-2000||11:40 PM||||It depends.  Sometimes I want something really bad, so I think to myself that I can just wait until there are only 5 min. left and then bid.  Well, that doesn't always work because I forget.  However when I remember I manage to get stuff that way all the time, and pretty cheap.<P>People used to do that to me all the time, now I make sure I am online when the auction closes just so no one will outbid me with 5 min. left or whatever, especially with an auction with a lot of bids...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||12-08-2000||03:20 AM||||I have lost a few items within the last minute of bidding. If you want try looking on Yahoo Auctions for the parts. Less bids, lower prices. Usually I sell on Ebay but if I'm looking for something I try Yahoo first.<BR>If you play it right you could buy stuff on Yahoo and sell on Ebay for a profit! I always check the net or local shops prior to bidding. I was going to bid on an air compressor for an air brush, On Ebay the model and size I was looking for usually sold for about $140.00. I searched the net and found an Art supply place selling it on sale for $89.99 and with free shipping for the month of December! (It'll be here on Tuesday!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||12-08-2000||06:54 AM||||I called my local bike shop and they told me the head gasket was $40 and this guy has all top end gaskets for $20+ .Just hope my ebay works .I have never used it. As long as i have a username and password and have registered i can bid right?<BR>Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||12-08-2000||07:06 AM||||Correct, that's all you need to be able to bid.  Since you know what parts from a supply house cost, make sure you factor in what shipping will be as you bid on the ebay item.||||reg||1
Z||000006||hugh||12-08-2000||07:41 AM||||$40 for a head gasket.That sounds like list price +.I believe you have to also have a credit card registered with E bay. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||12-08-2000||08:24 AM||||Something you see on Ebay, will always be on Ebay again, dont think it will be your only chance to get it.<P>There have been things i wanted, and sometimes later on someone has a better deal or they include more items with it.<P>Motorcycle parts always varies, i sometimes bought some things for my bike, honda dealerships cost way to much for parts.  But there is always someone parting out their bike and selling parts.  Dont bid to much when you know its not that costly someplace else.  If its a 1903 motorcycle gasket and its orignal go for it, otherwise think about it first, or go to a salvage yard.||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||12-09-2000||01:48 AM||||hugh, you only need a credit card registered on eBay if you are a seller - a buyer need not register a credit card but they do need a user name and password to use the system.||||reg||1
